# ASDD frontmatter — read by `asdd/ai-workflow/` skills.
# Do NOT remove; edit to match your setup.

asdd_profile: be

# Base branch used by pr-handoff (fallback: development).
base_branch: development

# Ticketing system used by ticket-author and pr-handoff.
ticketing:
  system: azure-devops       # or: github-issues, jira, linear, gitlab
  ticket_id_pattern: "#<NUMBER>"   # examples: "#1234", "PROJ-1234", "GH-1234"
---

# AGENTS.md

Shared baseline instructions for AI coding agents working on the
**<Project name>** repository. Keep this file lean.

## Project Overview

<Describe what this project is in 3–5 lines: the main product, the primary
consumers (FE app, integrations), the runtime target, the top 3 tools
anyone touching the codebase must be aware of.>

Example baseline (edit to match your project):

> `<Project name>` is a **C# / .NET 10** REST API for <domain>. It exposes
> the <domain> to the `<Project name>` frontend and to internal integrations,
> using **EF Core** on SQL Server, **Azure AD** authentication
> (`Microsoft.Identity.Web` in dev, EasyAuth in prod), and Azure DevOps for
> CI/CD.

## Project Layout — Non-Obvious Bits

- **Solution:** `<Project>/<Project>.sln` — three projects:
  - `<Project>` (Web / API host).
  - `<Project>.Core` (Domain + Services + Interfaces + Core DTOs).
  - `<Project>.DAL` (EF Core context + Repositories).
- **Layering (strict):** Controller (Web) → Service (`Core/Services`,
  registered via `ServicesInitializer`) → Repository (`DAL/Repositories`,
  registered via `RepositoriesInitializer`) → EF Core `<Name>DbContext`.
  No DB calls from controllers. No business logic in controllers.
- **DTO placement:** Web DTOs in `<Project>/DTOs/Requests` and
  `<Project>/DTOs/Responses`; Core DTOs in `<Project>.Core/DTOs`. Never leak
  an entity through the HTTP boundary.
- **Mapping:** AutoMapper via `<Project>/Mapper/ApiProfile.cs` (Web ↔ Core).
- **URL segments in kebab-case**, enforced by
  `<Project>/Utils/KebabCaseParameterTransformer.cs`.
- **API docs:** Swagger / Swashbuckle at `/swagger` (`AddSwaggerGen` in
  `Program.cs`).

## Domain Core

Three concepts that cannot be inferred from the code alone (edit to match
your domain):

- **<Term>** — <one-line definition>.
- **<Term>** — <one-line definition>.
- **<Term>** — <one-line definition>.

## Tooling

- **Language / runtime:** C# on **.NET 10**
  (`<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>`), `Nullable enable`,
  `ImplicitUsings enable`.
- **Persistence:** EF Core 10 on SQL Server
  (`Microsoft.Data.SqlClient`); single `DbContext`
  (`<Project>.DAL/Data/<Name>DbContext.cs`); `dotnet-ef` 10.0.9.
- **Auth (dev):** JWT Bearer via `Microsoft.Identity.Web` / Azure AD (see
  `Program.cs`, `AzureAd` config section).
- **Auth (prod):** EasyAuth (Azure App Service Authentication) via
  `<Project>/Auth/EasyAuthHandler.cs` +
  `<Project>/Auth/EasyAuthMiddleware.cs`.
- **Claims:** `<Project>/Auth/AzureAdClaimsTransformation.cs`, helpers in
  `<Project>/Auth/ClaimsExtensions.cs`, `<Project>/Auth/CurrentUser.cs`.
- **Authorization policies:** declared in `<Project>/Auth/Policies/*`
  (`AdminPolicies`, `AccessLevelPolicies`, `EnvironmentPolicies`, …),
  central names in `<Project>/Auth/Policies/PolicyNames.cs`.
  **Every endpoint must carry an `[Authorize(Policy = PolicyNames.X)]`
  unless it is genuinely public.**
- **Context7 MCP** — use it for any library, framework, SDK, or API
  documentation, setup, configuration, or CLI usage. Don't wait to be asked.

## Basic Project Commands

```bash
dotnet restore
dotnet build ./<Project>/<Project>.sln -c Release
dotnet test  ./<Project>/<Project>.sln -s ./<Project>/<Project>.Tests/test.runsettings

# Schema changes (only when the migrations flow is confirmed for the ticket)
dotnet ef migrations add <Name> --project <Project>.DAL --startup-project <Project>
```

Runtime configuration source: `appsettings.json`,
`appsettings.Development.example.json` (template),
`appsettings.Production.json`. `appsettings.Development.json` is
git-ignored.

## Testing

- **xUnit** + Moq + `Moq.AutoMock` + FluentAssertions + AutoFixture +
  coverlet.
- Projects under `<Project>.Tests/` (`Core.Tests`, `DAL.Tests`,
  `Backend.Tests`). Some DAL tests hit a real SQL Server via
  `test.runsettings` env vars (e.g. `<PROJECT>_TEST_CONNECTION_STRING`).
- **Layer isolation.** Service tests mock the repository interface; do not
  spin up the DbContext.
- **`[ProducesResponseType]`** attributes must match the tested status
  codes; controller tests cross-check that mapping.

## Code Conventions

### Layering & DTO placement

- **Layering discipline:** Controller → Service → Repository (or the repo's
  variant). No cross-layer leaks. No DB calls from controllers. No business
  logic in controllers.
- **DTO placement:** Web DTOs in the Web project's `DTOs/{Requests,Responses}`;
  Core DTOs in the Core project's `DTOs`. Never leak an entity through the
  HTTP boundary.
- **Mapping:** additions to the AutoMapper `ApiProfile` (or the declared
  mapping profile), not ad-hoc mapping in controllers.
- **Auth:** never propose an endpoint without an
  `[Authorize(Policy = PolicyNames.X)]` unless the ticket explicitly
  justifies it as public.

### API conventions (routing, response types, idempotency)

- **REST** with `[ApiController]` + `[Route("api/...")]`.
- **URL segments in kebab-case**, enforced by
  `<Project>/Utils/KebabCaseParameterTransformer.cs`.
- **Kebab-case routing** — action names respect the declared style; only
  flag if a custom `[HttpXxx("literal-name")]` breaks the pattern.
- **Status codes** documented per action via `[ProducesResponseType(...)]`;
  200 / 201 / 204 on success paths.
- **`[ProducesResponseType]`** — every documented status code must be
  declared.
- **Idempotency** — no repo-wide convention. Idempotency rules must be
  declared per endpoint in the ticket's `Contracts & Specs`.

### Error envelope (uniform)

Errors flow through `<Project>/Handlers/GlobalExceptionHandler.cs`:

```jsonc
{
  "message": "<ERROR_CODE_OR_TEXT>",
  "statusCode": 400,
  "isHandled": true,
  "errors": null
}
```

Mapping:

| Status | Exception type                                                          |
|--------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| 400    | `ValidationException`, `ArgumentException`, `InvalidOperationException` |
| 401    | `UnauthorizedAccessException`                                           |
| 403    | `Forbidden*` exceptions                                                 |
| 404    | `NotFoundException`                                                     |
| 409    | domain-specific conflict exceptions                                     |
| 422    | `ConfigurationValidationException` (fills `errors`)                     |
| 500    | anything else                                                           |

**Do not** return bespoke error shapes from a controller. Throw the typed
exception; the handler applies the envelope.

### Persistence & migrations

- Single `<Name>DbContext` in `<Project>.DAL/Data/`.
- Entities in `<Project>.Core/Entities/`.
- **Migrations:** if the DAL does not currently ship a `Migrations/`
  folder, the schema-change flow is an **open convention**. Until it is
  decided, `asdd/ai-workflow/skills/repo-viability-scan.md` treats any schema
  change as `RED` and escalates.

### Style

- **Lint / format:** only compiler + nullable warnings today; no additional
  analyzer / editorconfig detected. Do **not** suppress warnings to make a
  build green.
- **Comments:** the agent honors the minimal-comments rule
  ([`asdd/ai-workflow/AGENTS.md` → Rule #6](../asdd/ai-workflow/AGENTS.md)).
  Inline comments only when genuinely necessary; file-header of ≤3 lines
  is the only agent-initiated comment allowed.

## Commit & PR Conventions

- **Base branch:** `development` (or per `base_branch` in the frontmatter).
- **Branch prefixes:** `feature/*`, `fix/*`, `chore/*`.
- **Commit format** — Conventional Commits with the ticket ID at the end:

  ```text
  <type>(<scope>): <imperative summary> (#<TICKET-ID>)
  ```

  - **Allowed types:** `feat | fix | docs | style | refactor | test |
    chore | perf | ci | build | revert`.
  - Description is imperative and short.
  - Message references the ticket ID (e.g. `(#1234)`).
- **One ticket → one focused PR.**
- **PR must trigger** the repo's PR checks (e.g.
  `.pipelines/pr-checks/build-check.yml`).
- **No `--force` on shared branches.**
- **No `--no-verify`.**

## What NOT to Do

- **Do not bump the language / runtime version** without an explicit ticket.
- **Do not add ad-hoc error shapes** — throw the typed exception; let the
  global handler apply the envelope.
- **Do not add DB calls in controllers** — go through a service.
- **Do not leak an entity through a controller** — map to a DTO.
- **Do not skip `[Authorize(Policy = PolicyNames.X)]`** unless the endpoint
  is genuinely public and justified.
- **Do not skip `[ProducesResponseType]`** for documented status codes.
- **Do not add inline comments** to generated code except when genuinely
  necessary, when they carry important non-obvious context, or when the
  user explicitly asked. Only a **file-header block of at most 3 lines**
  may be added on the agent's initiative. See
  [`asdd/ai-workflow/AGENTS.md` → Rule #6](../asdd/ai-workflow/AGENTS.md)
  for the full rule; do not restate it here.
- **Do not add a migration without a confirmed migrations flow** —
  escalate.
- **Do not suppress warnings, delete tests, or narrow scope** to make a
  build green.
- **Do not push directly to the base branch** or force-push shared branches.
- **Do not commit with `--no-verify`.**
